# Rule: Stitch to React Native production migration

Read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/design/stitch-react-native-rules.md` before editing mobile UI.

- Stitch controls visual appearance only. Backend business rules, authorization, and OpenAPI control behavior and wire data.
- Replace screens incrementally and remove old presentation code only after all callers move and no business logic is lost.
- Never import HTML/CSS/Tailwind/DOM into React Native or use WebView as a conversion shortcut.
- Keep production API integration, secure session storage, UUID identity, server pagination, idempotency, private media authorization, and truthful error states.
- Fixtures are development-preview-only and never a runtime fallback.
- Do not run verification commands or commit/push unless the user explicitly requests it.
- Report `IMPLEMENTED_UNVERIFIED` until the user supplies verification evidence.
